IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wica-types`
IMPORT `wica-schedules`
IMPORT `wica-liability`

-- Work Injury Compensation Act 2019 — TESTS FOR GOALS 1 AND 2: coverage and
-- liability (accidents, platform operators' shares, the principal, disease).
--
-- Every expected value is worked from ../source/WICA2019.txt; the section
-- or Schedule item is on each assertion. The records below are a base case
-- (an employee, born 10 March 1996, hurt at work in Singapore on 2 March
-- 2026) and one change per scenario.

§ `Tests — Goals 1 and 2`

§§ `Helpers`

GIVEN c IS A `Coverage`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `covered:` c IF
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `not covered` r THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN l IS A `Liability`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `liable:` l IF
    CONSIDER l
    WHEN `liable to pay compensation` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN d IS A `Disease liability`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `compensable:` d IF
    CONSIDER d
    WHEN `compensable as if a work injury` u THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN who IS A STRING, shares IS A LIST OF `Operator share`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the share of` who `among` shares MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN s YIELD s's `share`) (filter (GIVEN s YIELD s's `operator` EQUALS who) shares))

GIVEN who IS A STRING, st IS A `Work stage`, earned IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Platform engagement`
`engaged with` who `at` st `earning` earned MEANS
    `Platform engagement` WITH `operator` IS who, `stage` IS st, `earnings in the lookback period` IS earned

§§ `Claimants`

-- the base case: an employee under a contract of service, in no Third Schedule class
`an employee` MEANS Claimant WITH
    `name` IS "Tan"
    `date of birth` IS YMD 1996 3 10
    `capacity` IS `as an employee`
    `works under a contract of service` IS TRUE
    `works under a platform work agreement` IS FALSE
    `class` IS `none of the Third Schedule classes`
    `a Government employee` IS FALSE
    `in a class the President has declared` IS FALSE
    `the contract was illegal at the time of the accident` IS FALSE
    `ordinarily resident in Singapore` IS TRUE
    `employed by an employer in Singapore` IS TRUE
    `required by the employment to work outside Singapore` IS FALSE
    `employed as crew of a Singapore ship` IS FALSE

