§§ `Accidents`

-- the base case: in Singapore, in the course of the work, on 2 March 2026
`at work` MEANS Accident WITH
    `date` IS YMD 2026 3 2
    `in Singapore` IS TRUE
    `on a Singapore ship` IS FALSE
    `in the course of the work` IS TRUE
    `evidence it did not arise out of the work` IS FALSE
    `travelling as a passenger to or from the workplace with the employer's permission` IS FALSE
    `transport operated by or for the employer, or by arrangement with the employer` IS FALSE
    `transport operated in the ordinary course of a public transport service` IS FALSE
    `in or about the workplace, or at work providing the platform service` IS FALSE
    `taking steps in an actual or supposed emergency to rescue, protect or avert damage` IS FALSE
    `acting in contravention of law, regulations or orders, or without instructions` IS FALSE
    `would otherwise have arisen out of and in the course of the work` IS FALSE
    `the act was done for the purposes of and in connection with the business or service` IS FALSE
    `proven the injury is directly attributable to alcohol or a drug` IS FALSE
    `deliberate self-injury or deliberate aggravation` IS FALSE
    `injured in a fight or an assault` IS FALSE
    `assaulted another person in the fight` IS FALSE
    `any assault was in the exercise of the right of private defence` IS FALSE
    `breaking up or preventing the fight, or safeguarding life, property or law and order` IS FALSE
    `under the instruction or with the consent of the employer or platform operator` IS FALSE
    `proven contravention of a Sixth Schedule Part 1 law in using a vehicle` IS FALSE
    `used a vehicle in providing the platform service` IS FALSE
    `proven contravention of a Sixth Schedule Part 2 law about that vehicle` IS FALSE
    `proven that contravention caused or contributed to the accident` IS FALSE
    `platform engagements` IS EMPTY

